// This is a binary file (PNG image) that needs to be copied from the project root to the assets directory.
// In Angular CLI projects, static assets should be placed in the src/assets folder.

// Migration steps:
// 1. Create the directory structure if it doesn't exist:
//    mkdir -p src/assets/images
//
// 2. Copy the file:
//    cp project-logo.png src/assets/images/
//
// 3. When referencing this image in Angular components, use:
//    imageUrl = 'assets/images/project-logo.png';
//
// 4. In HTML templates:
//    <img [src]="imageUrl" alt="Project Logo">
//    or directly:
//    <img src="assets/images/project-logo.png" alt="Project Logo">
//
// 5. Update any references to this image in your application
//    from '/project-logo.png' to '/assets/images/project-logo.png'